{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210731,"nonce":"h25Pbel47A8vGXkK/s+TzdEw9h8=","title":"AOT liveness pass missed CrossFnCall args dropped by the Phase 1 split","message":"Fixed in commit d4ac2c4. Record migrated from session memory 2026-09-12.\n\n**RESOLVED at HEAD `d4ac2c4` (2026-05-18).**\n\n\nSite's `App.serve_(_)` (8 cross-fn yields, results flowing through the second half) rejected with `\"uses value vN from non-dominating instM\"`. Same pattern in closure_6 (large multi-yield bodies).\n\n\nPhase 1 of the SM transform drops the suspension `Call` instruction during the block split. That removes the call's `receiver` + `args` operands from the MIR. The liveness pass in Phase 2 only walks MIR instructions + terminators, so it couldn't see those uses — and any value flowing only from pre-yield-K into yield K+1's call args got dropped from saves[K].\n\nDownstream, the cranelift backend's CrossFnCallInit save_arg sequence at yield K+1's yielding-block would read `val_map[arg_vid]` of a vid that's only bound in a sibling block (yield K's resume's done-branch). That sibling block doesn't dominate the dispatcher-direct br_table resume paths, so the cranelift verifier rejects.\n\n\n`compute_saves_loads` now feeds each `CrossFnCall`'s `receiver` + `args` into a new `extra_uses` table before running liveness, via `compute_all_live_in_with_extra(mir, extra_uses)`. Values flowing across multiple yields now properly chain through saves[K] → loads[K+1].\n\n\n- 21/21 aot_runtime\n- 113/113 e2e (modulo pre-existing parallel-only flakes)\n- 36/36 events.spec (was BUILD-FAIL)\n- 30/33 proc.spec (was BUILD-FAIL)\n- 24/25 http.spec\n- Hatch site AOT-compiles cleanly, boots, listens on :3000 (was: total verifier reject)\n\n\nThese are downstream of cap-3 in nested-cross-fn shapes; the SM transform itself is now sound:\n\n1. **Streaming readers (`Reader.withTryFn` pattern)** — 1 fail each in proc.spec / io.spec / http.spec. Same shape: multi-yield-in-loop with chunked-byte stream protocol. Likely needs investigation of how `try`-based reader loops interact with cross-fn cloning.\n\n2. **Catalog fetch (nested `Fiber.new` + `driveFiberValue_`)** — site boots but catalog HTTP fetch returns null. The pattern is `Fiber.new(Fn.new { Http.get(url) }, 1024).try()` driven by an outer fiber. Likely Mechanism B (silently-dropped FiberAction::Yield) somewhere in the foreign-method chain; would surface as a hard error if Phase 5 of the original plan (turning Mechanism B into a panic) was implemented.\n\nHow to apply: when these resurface, the SM transform is correct — look upstream/downstream of the transform.","files":null}]}